 "about": "The dated facts about voice design, text to speech, voice changing, lip sync, music and sound-effect tools, with their consent gates and commercial terms (blueprint 8.2, 8.6; D3, D9). Checked 2026-09-27.",
 "how_to_read": [
  "voice: tools that make or change speech; lip_sync: tools that fit a mouth to a take afterwards; music and effects: generators, video-to-audio models and libraries.",
  "commercial and film_use: whether the output may go into a film that is shown or sold (D4; D9 rule 9). A tool whose terms exclude film is never budgeted (D13 R19).",
  "consent_gate: what the tool demands before a real person's voice is copied. The kit's own rule is stricter: never a celebrity, a child or a dead person, and never from existing recordings (D3 rule 16).",
  "path_treatments: the saved treatment for each path a voice takes (earpiece, radio, intercom ...), applied in the edit, never asked of a video model (D3 rule 24).",
  "marks: V verified, V-sec secondary, U unverified, J judgement, with the research file's section and source."
 ],
